\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.3}{\ignorespaces The Department of Computer Science has the biggest elective program of Industrial Experience (IE) at the University of Manchester. The chart shows the number of students starting an Industrial Experience placement year in 2024 as part of their undergraduate study at the University of Manchester. The data is plotted by Department: \texttt  {CS}: Department of Computer Science \href  {https://www.cs.manchester.ac.uk/}{cs.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {MACE}: Department of Mechanical, Aerospace and Civil Engineering (MACE) \href  {https://www.mace.manchester.ac.uk/}{mace.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {EEE}: Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering \href  {https://www.eee.manchester.ac.uk/}{eee.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {ChemEng}: Department of Chemical Engineering \href  {https://www.ce.manchester.ac.uk/}{ce.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {Chemistry}: Department of Chemistry \href  {https://www.chemistry.manchester.ac.uk/}{chemistry.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {Maths}: Department of Mathematics \href  {https://www.maths.manchester.ac.uk}{maths.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {Physics}: Department of Physics \& Astronomy \href  {https://www.physics.manchester.ac.uk}{physics.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {Materials}: Department of Materials \href  {https://www.materials.manchester.ac.uk/}{materials.manchester.ac.uk}, \texttt  {EES}: Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences \href  {https://www.ees.manchester.ac.uk/}{ees.manchester.ac.uk}. Data from PowerBI as of 2025, note that summer internships are shown in this bar chart, only year long placements.}}{43}{figure.8.3}\protected@file@percent }
